ft" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Average</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1.67 (0.93 to 3.00) <italic>p</italic> = 0.088</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">NA<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tfn15-ehp-116-1396">c</xref></td></tr></tbody></table><table-wrap-foot><fn id="tfn12-ehp-116-1396"><p>NA, not available.</p></fn><fn id="tfn13-ehp-116-1396"><label>a</label><p>Model included cord lead level, sex, gestational age, maternal education, and ETS as covariates.</p></fn><fn id="tfn14-ehp-116-1396"><label>b</label><p>The ORs for cord adducts presented in this table represent the effect of a 1-unit (0.1 adduct/10<sup>8</sup> nucleotides) increment in cord adducts.</p></fn><fn id="tfn15-ehp-116-1396"><label>c</label><p>SPSS statistical software (SPSS Inc, Chicago, IL, USA) failed to provide accurate estimates.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap></floats-wrap></article>